Australian Product Guide — Brand Fidelity v32.2 certified presentation release
Release date: 2026-08-18
Status: CURRENT / PRODUCTION VERIFIED / EXACT-SHA VISUAL CERTIFIED
Production source: GitHub main via Vercel
Canonical production domain: https://australianproductguide.au

Current platform: the underlying APG application/data capability remains the maintained priority-commerce / Decision Intelligence v4.1 / Evidence & Commerce Depth v27 / Trust Infrastructure v28 / Amazon Conversion v29 stack, with Premium Brand v30, Premium Theme v31.1 and Brand Fidelity v32.2 forming the current controlling presentation system. The architecture remains lightweight SSR-first Node with progressive enhancement. v32.2 is a presentation and visual-certification release; it does not change product-fit logic, catalogue data, retailer ranking, affiliate weighting, account/auth behaviour or privacy controls.

Brand-fidelity truth: the owner-approved APG brand board is now implemented as a coherent production identity rather than an approximate A-shaped logo. The current mark uses the traced four-part APG geometry and first-party responsive identity assets for primary horizontal, compact, APG monogram, standalone symbol, white, monochrome, favicon, app-icon and social applications. Desktop uses the full Australian Product Guide lock-up. Standard tablet/mobile widths use the APG symbol/monogram relationship, with the monogram P explicitly kept white on navy so the mark remains fully legible. Very narrow layouts may simplify further without distorting the master mark.

Colour-system truth: the controlling palette is APG Blue #2563EB, APG Navy #0F172A, APG Teal #06B6D4, APG Green #10B981, Light Grey #F1F5F9 and Slate #64748B, supported by white and accessible light/dark text tokens. Navy is used for institutional authority and deep surfaces; blue is the primary action colour; teal/green remain selective accents; white/light grey provide breathing space. Dark surfaces use white or sufficiently light foreground text rather than low-contrast navy/grey combinations.

Maintained-research highlight: the successful historical yellow treatment was recovered from APG source history rather than guessed. The current MAINTAINED AUSTRALIAN RESEARCH band uses #FFD65B → #F4BB45 → #F2B348, with #E0A630/#D89C24 border tones and #082735 foreground text. Yellow remains a strategic high-attention trust accent rather than a primary site colour. The banner's product/category/brand values remain data-driven from the authoritative maintained catalogue rather than hard-coded release numbers.

Catalogue and commerce snapshot at certification: live observability reported 482 maintained products, 90 populated categories and 178 canonical represented brands. Exact Australian retailer/manufacturer coverage was 52 verified destinations across 46 products from 20 sources, comprising 41 independent-retailer observations and 11 manufacturer-direct observations. The Amazon Australia path remains available across the maintained catalogue, with 22 independently verified exact Amazon identities and transparent model-specific search fallbacks where exact identity is not verified. Affiliate participation, retailer availability and commission contribute zero recommendation points.

Imagery truth: verified external exact-model product photography remains 0/482 in the governed registry. APG continues to use first-party/category-correct authored decision visuals where authorised exact product photography is unavailable. APG does not scrape Amazon product pages, reverse-engineer image URLs, fabricate real-product photography or claim third-party imagery rights it does not hold. Authorised image delivery remains a separate ingestion task.

Scout identity: Scout remains APG's decision-assistance product and now uses the APG Blue + white master symbol consistently in the launcher, panel avatar and conversational avatar after JavaScript initialisation. v32.2 includes a small runtime identity guard so the legacy mascot cannot overwrite the approved APG mark after page load. Scout decision logic, structured-session continuity and the zero-commercial-weight recommendation controls are unchanged.

Responsive and accessibility truth: the final visual system was inspected separately across desktop, tablet and mobile. The release strengthens dark/light surface contrast, keeps the responsive APG monogram readable, preserves the distinctive yellow proof band, prevents true document-width overflow, retains readable footer/trust typography and keeps product, comparison, search, Decision Lab, My APG and Scout surfaces visually coherent without turning the whole site dark. Legitimate internally scrollable comparison/research content is not incorrectly treated as page overflow.

Release history and verification: PR #79, Finish APG v32 brand fidelity across mobile and Scout, merged the certified implementation to GitHub main at bd60ad3c5aabfc139eb4e0b23ea005149c4eadcc. All 28 affected pull-request regression workflows passed before merge, including Brand Fidelity, Decision Intelligence, Amazon, retailer depth, platform integrity/cohesion, account/auth/governance, source, product-image, mobile and premium-theme controls. Vercel Production deployment dpl_77cMJNaBirdYSgcfa5JUo24hUx1d is READY in syd1 and aliases australianproductguide.au. Canonical Production returned HTTP 200 with the v32.2 runtime/assets and the current data-driven maintained-research values.

Exact-Production visual certification: APG v32 Brand Visual Certification run 32126054082 passed the exact-SHA wait, v32.2 public-contract and Decision Lab SSR checks, desktop/tablet/mobile render matrix, current-main recheck and screenshot-artifact publication. It certified 32 Production visual states covering homepage, search, category, product, comparison, Decision Lab shell/results, My APG, trust/privacy, open Scout and responsive navigation. Artifact 9320416716 is retained until 17 September 2026; failures.json is empty. APG v27 Visual Certification run 32126054062 also passed on the same implementation SHA. Manual review of the final screenshots confirmed the mobile APG monogram, APG-branded Scout, yellow research band, major decision/purchase surfaces and footer/trust treatments were visually coherent and readable.

Remaining external gaps: lawful genuine-product photography ingestion remains incomplete until an authorised delivery/right basis exists. Hosted Supabase Auth settings that are outside the connected writable surface, including the previously identified leaked-password-protection setting, remain separate owner/admin configuration work unless subsequently verified otherwise. Formal trade mark clearance/registration is not claimed by this release.

Release discipline: GitHub main remains authoritative and Vercel Production must match it. The implementation baseline certified above is bd60ad3c5aabfc139eb4e0b23ea005149c4eadcc. This release-record reconciliation is documentation-only; once merged, the resulting main SHA must itself receive a READY Production deployment and exact-commit visual certification before the record update is treated as fully reconciled.